WEBVTT

00:01.901 --> 00:03.103
I am Danny.

00:03.103 --> 00:04.904
Danny Pascal.

00:04.904 --> 00:06.906
I'm originally from London.

00:06.906 --> 00:08.875
And this is my wife.

00:08.875 --> 00:10.143
This.

00:10.143 --> 00:11.978
I'm Tunisian Pascal.

00:11.978 --> 00:13.646
I am originally.

00:13.646 --> 00:16.049
I'm from Guyana, South America.

00:16.049 --> 00:21.654
And I moved to London
and then I'm in Wales now.

00:21.755 --> 00:25.525
We spoke about moving to the country
maybe ten years ago.

00:25.759 --> 00:27.193
Isn't it? Yeah.

00:27.193 --> 00:31.097
It's like stepping out of London,
and I never thought I would leave.

00:31.264 --> 00:33.400
Yeah, it was hard in this one, too.

00:33.400 --> 00:34.934
But I was not assigned to anywhere.

00:34.934 --> 00:36.136
I could live anywhere.

00:36.136 --> 00:38.972
I already left Canada and,

00:38.972 --> 00:41.274
I mean,
I guess you could say we're farmers.

00:41.274 --> 00:42.709
We have our own business.

00:42.709 --> 00:43.843
A farm, skin care.

00:43.843 --> 00:46.312
We make our own
natural skin skincare products.

00:46.312 --> 00:51.051
And we came to the farm to grow
those ingredients.

00:51.151 --> 00:51.684
mom and dad.

00:51.684 --> 00:53.086
Born and raised in London.

00:53.086 --> 00:55.255
They're 67 now.

00:55.255 --> 00:55.588
They.

00:55.588 --> 00:58.124
They don't know this life, you know?

00:58.124 --> 01:01.394
So then for them to pass that on through
generations

01:01.394 --> 01:05.298
would be impossible
unless they made that that decision to.

01:05.465 --> 01:08.768
To change their trajectory,
which, you know, they had no reason to

01:08.802 --> 01:10.336
they had no or no desire to.

01:10.336 --> 01:13.706
You know, they may have been small desires
like my mom getting the allotment

01:13.706 --> 01:17.010
that was you know,
that was something that she took from

01:17.110 --> 01:21.881
going to visit her uncle in Birmingham,
who was directly from Jamaica.

01:21.948 --> 01:23.650
So there's an element of it.

01:23.650 --> 01:26.619
But then there was never
let's make this practical.

01:26.686 --> 01:30.023
And I don't mean specifically
getting into farming, just

01:30.123 --> 01:33.626
I guess being in the country,
being surrounded by nature.

01:33.726 --> 01:36.729
So his mum invited us
to like in one of the beds

01:36.830 --> 01:38.731
and I was like,
Oh, this is why I was missing

01:38.731 --> 01:39.566
hands in the soil,

01:39.566 --> 01:43.570
because we grew so much of our own food
at home and you knew the person

01:43.570 --> 01:45.205
who you were buying your food from,
you know, So

01:45.205 --> 01:47.574
everything was natural as organic,
you know, buying stuff

01:47.574 --> 01:50.543
in plastic bags that we just didn't
have that experience.

01:50.643 --> 01:54.247
You could never catch me living in London
again, like we love where we live.

01:54.347 --> 01:58.418
I want to smile, but I go back to
to London and I don't feel I can do that,

01:58.485 --> 01:59.452
you know what I mean?

01:59.452 --> 02:02.789
So and it's not something
that I would want for for our son,

02:02.789 --> 02:06.259
especially being a black boy where you can
where you grew up.

02:06.259 --> 02:11.998
And then all of a sudden you you feel
the need that you call hiding yourself.

02:12.065 --> 02:16.169
We've lived across this part of Wales

02:16.169 --> 02:20.607
for the last four years,
and it's been kind of the same experience,

02:20.673 --> 02:24.611
you know, of of good people,
friendly people generally.

02:24.711 --> 02:29.349
I also think of us being here
is showing people that they can do it.

02:29.449 --> 02:31.951
And it's a like unintentional thing of us
being here

02:31.951 --> 02:33.820
because we've come out and we're like,
Yeah, we can do it.

02:33.820 --> 02:35.355
You know, a lot of people would think,

02:35.355 --> 02:38.958
like with our son, because he's
the only black kid in a school

02:39.058 --> 02:41.394
and is he going to get bullied?

02:41.394 --> 02:44.097
Might he get called a name? Probably.

02:44.097 --> 02:46.666
Is the same thing
more likely to happen in London

02:46.666 --> 02:49.302
or will it as likely happen in London?

02:49.302 --> 02:50.470
Probably.

02:50.470 --> 02:54.374
So life away in those things
up, I'm like, yeah,

02:54.374 --> 02:55.708
he can run on the beach,

02:55.708 --> 02:59.145
he can climb hills,
he can run around with his sheep, he can

02:59.245 --> 03:02.815
we can build him a friggin tree house
like he has all of these things that help

03:02.849 --> 03:06.786
ground him as a human being.

03:06.853 --> 03:08.788
And for me, that's more important

03:08.788 --> 03:13.092
than focusing on the color of his skin
and then staying in a place

03:13.193 --> 03:15.929
just so that he can see
all the people who look like him.

03:15.929 --> 03:20.066
Because as his parents, it's our job
to instill the pride

03:20.166 --> 03:23.336
and the cultural relevance and show him

03:23.336 --> 03:27.040
how beautiful it is that his ancestors
made a way for him to be here

03:27.106 --> 03:30.610
and to have that freedom
of being a human being on this planet

03:30.677 --> 03:35.281
is something about just being able
to look instead of over the horizon

03:35.281 --> 03:38.651
and see these rolling hills
and just see nature play out,

03:38.685 --> 03:40.320
especially throughout the year,

03:40.320 --> 03:43.022
you know, because when spring summer comes
and you see butterflies come out

03:43.022 --> 03:48.661
and on this farm with foxes and badgers,
rabbits, rabbits, it's so cute.

03:48.828 --> 03:50.730
And it's just
I mean, it's literally a Disney film.

03:50.730 --> 03:55.068
Sometimes you can walk around here
and be like, This is crazy.

03:55.168 --> 03:56.903
And and that's a beautiful thing.

03:56.903 --> 04:00.807
We can literally just sit at this table
and look out that window for a day and

04:00.940 --> 04:02.709
and be quite content.

04:02.709 --> 04:05.144
You know, you finally get to be
the hermit. You've always wanted to be.

04:05.144 --> 04:06.079
Exactly. Yeah.
